{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115114","id":3186243488,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc696jeg","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115114","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115114.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115114.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115114","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115114/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115114/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115114/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6ff5f449a952d151b187c62b3a46490a02ec25b2","number":115114,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add support for the Home LED on NS Controllers","user":{"login":"ThiLelito","id":125714191,"node_id":"U_kgDOB34_Dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125714191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito","html_url":"https://github.com/ThiLelito","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"With the addition of `Input.set_joy_light()` from [#111681](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111681), I wondered if the LED around the Home Button in some Nintendo Switch controllers could be adjusted. I discovered they could not, because its implementation uses the `SDL_SetJoystickLED` function while the Home LED uses the `SDL_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_SWITCH_HOME_LED` hint.\r\n\r\nThis PR aims to add support for this LED mentioned.\r\n\r\nI only changed the `drivers/sdl/joypad_sdl.cpp` file:\r\n\r\n- Added an if condition on `close_joypad` to check if it's a NS controller and turn the LED off if true:\r\n  - Sets the `SDL_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_SWITCH_HOME_LED` hint to `\"0.0\"`;\r\n- Added an if condition on `has_joy_light` to make NS controllers `return true`;\r\n- Added logic to set up the brightness of the NS controller LED:\r\n  - It gets the max rgb value of the Color provided;\r\n  - Sets the `SDL_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_SWITCH_HOME_LED` hint with the `char *` of the maximum value.\r\n\r\nI've tested on Windows and it seems to work. I don't know if there are other controllers that use the same hint and are not mentioned in the if statements. If so, feel free to change or improve it.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471795,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE3OTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:thirdparty","name":"topic:thirdparty","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://gith